          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Kontsevich integral
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dyson+formula"} Dyson formula
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+configuration+spaces+of+points"} ordered configuration spaces of points
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+Vassiliev+invariant"} universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+invariant"} Vassiliev invariant
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braids"} braids
            and, with due care, of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knots"} knots
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/links"} links
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop+observable"} Wilson loop observable
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} perturbatively quantized
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            The Kontsevich integral generalises the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss+integral+formula"} Gauss integral formula
            which computes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linking+number"} linking number
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circles"} circles
            via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#OnBraids On braids
          %div
            %p
              For the Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnection"}
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
              we need the following notation:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{\mathrm{f}} \in \mathbb{N}
                  write
                #eq:OrderedConfigurationSpaceofnPointsinC.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi Conf
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi N
                                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo \
                        %mi FatDiagonal
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{R}^2)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        (\mathbb{R}^2)^n \backslash FatDiagonal
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+configuration+space+of+n+points"} ordered configuration space of n points
                  in the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                %p
                  Identifying the plane with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℂ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
                #eq:CoordinateFunctionsOnConfC.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mi Conf
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (z_1, \cdots, z_{N_{\mathrm{f}}})
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,n\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{R}^2)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathbb{C}^{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
                #eq:HorizontalChordDiagrams.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒜
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi pb
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Span
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒟
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi pb
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 4
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        Span\big(\mathcal{D}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}\big)/4T
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+vector+space"} quotient vector space
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  strands by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4T+relations"} 4T relations
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+braid+relations"}> infinitesimal braid relations
                  ), regarded as an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                  under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concatenation"} concatenation
                  of strands (
                  %a{:href => "horizontal+chord+diagram#AlgebraOfHorizontalChordDiagrams"}> here
                  ).
            #KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnection.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+form"}> Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov form
                  )
              %p
                The
                %em
                  universal
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+form"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov form
                is the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} algebra valued differential form
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HorizontalChordDiagrams"} (3)
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:OrderedConfigurationSpaceofnPointsinC"} (1)
              #eq:UniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KZ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi pb
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\omega_{KZ}
                      \\;\in\;
                      \\Omega
                      \\big(
                      \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{C})
                      \\,,
                      \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      \\big)
              %p
                given in the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CoordinateFunctionsOnConfC"} (2)
                by:
              #eq:DefineUniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KZ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\omega_{KZ}
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\underset{ i \lt j \in \{1, \cdots, n\} }{\sum}
                      d_{dR} log\big( z_i - z_j \big)
                      \\otimes t_{i j}
                      \\,,
              %p where
              %center
                %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HorizontalChordGenerator.jpg", :width => "500 /> "}/
              %p
                is the horizontal chord diagram with exactly one chord, which stretches between the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              %p
                Regarded as a connection form for a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+vector+bundle"} connection on a vector bundle
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∇
                          %mi KZ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_{KZ}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant derivative
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KV
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\nabla \phi
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      d \phi + \omega_{KV} \wedge \phi
              %p
                for any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi pb
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi \;\colon\;
                      \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{C})
                      \\longrightarrow
                      \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}} Mod
              %p
                with values in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                over the algebra of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} modulo
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4T+relations"} 4T relations
              %p The condition of covariant constancy
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mi KZ
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\nabla_{KZ} \phi \;=\; 0
              %p
                is called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov equation
              %p
                Finally, given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representations"} Lie algebra representations
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %msub
                        %mi Rep
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ∼
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (
                      V_1,
                      \\cdots,
                      V_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      )
                      \\;\in\; (\mathfrak{g} Rep_{/\sim})^{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      \\,,
              %p
                the corresponding
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi V
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi pf
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi End
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      w_{V}
                      \\;\colon\;
                      \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pf}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      \\longrightarrow
                      End_{\mathfrak{g}}\big( V_1 \otimes \cdots V_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}  \big)
              %p
                turns the universal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+form"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov form
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm"} (4)
                into a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+ring"} endomorphism ring
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} valued differential form
              #eq:LieKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KZ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\omega_{KZ}
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\underset{ i \lt j \in \{1, \cdots, n\} }{\sum}
                      d_{dR} log\big( z_i - z_j \big)
                      \\otimes w_V(t_{i j})
                      \\;\in\;
                      \\Omega
                      \\big(
                      \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{C})
                      \\,,
                      End\big(V_1 \otimes \cdot V_{N_{\mathrm{f}}} \big)
                      \\big)
                      
                      \\,.
            %p
              The universal formulation
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm"} (4)
              is highlighted for instance in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Vassiliev+invariant#BarNatan95"} Bat-Natan 95, Section 4.2
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Kontsevich+integral#Lescop00"} Lescop 00, p. 7
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Kontsevich+integral#Kohno14"} Kohno 14, Section 5
            #KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnectionIsFlat.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
                  is
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi ZK
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_{ZK}
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnection"}
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi ZK
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi ZK
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi ZK
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      d \omega_{ZK} + \omega_{ZK} \wedge \omega_{ZK}
                      \\;=\;
                      0
                      \\,.
            #KontsevichIntegralForBraids.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich+integral"} Kontsevich integral
                  for
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braids"} braids
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dyson+formula"} Dyson formula
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
                (Def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnection"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich+integral"} Kontsevich integral
                    on
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braids"} braids
            %p
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Kontsevich+integral#Lescop00"} Lescop 00, side-remark 1.14
          %h3#OnKnots On knots
          #kint.num_definition
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  strict Morse knot
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/strict+Morse+knot"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathcal{A}}
              be the
              %span.newWikiWord
                graded completion
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/graded+completion"} ?
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+chord+diagrams"} algebra of chord diagrams
              with
              = succeed "-term" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %strong Kontsevich integral
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is given by:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi m
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi min
                          %mo &lt;
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi m
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo &lt;
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mn 1
                          %mo &lt;
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi max
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi j
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtext non-critical
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi j
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mi P
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi p
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi m
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi j
                        %mo −
                        %mi d
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi j
                        %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi j
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mi j
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z(K)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\sum_{m = 0}^\infty \frac{1}{(2 \pi i)^m} \int_{t_{\min} \lt t_m \lt \cdots \lt t_1 \lt t_{\max} \over t_j\; \text{non-critical}} \sum_{P = \{(z_j,z_j')\}} (-1)^{\downarrow P} D_p \bigwedge_{j=1}^m \frac{d z_j - d z_j'}{z_j - z_j'}
          %p In this definition:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi min
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_{\min}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi max
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_{\max}
              are the minimum and maximum of the
              = succeed "-coordinate" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              %span.newWikiWord
                Morse knot
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Morse+knot"} ?
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              The integration is over the points in the simplex of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              points in the interval
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi min
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [t_{\min},t_{\max}]
              where no coordinate is critical on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              Upon removing the critical values (note:
              %em values
              not
              = succeed "," do
                %em points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \colon I \to \mathbb{C}
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is the corresponding interval of height values. In fact,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              must be the open interval between two successive critical values of the height function. For a particular such interval, there must be an even number of arcs with that domain. Given a point in the simplex (with no critical values), each coordinate in that point lies in an interval between critical values, and then for that interval we choose an unordered pair of arcs. A choice of pair for each coordinate is called a
              = succeed "," do
                %strong pairing
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi j
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \coloneqq \{(z_j,z_j')\}
            %li
              For a pairing,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \downarrow P
              denotes the number of arcs that are oriented downwards when equipped with the inherited orientation from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              Putting the knot back together as a circle, we join the ends of the pairing to make a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"} chord diagram
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              chords. This defines an element in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+chord+diagrams"} algebra of chord diagrams
              which we denote by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_P
          %h2#invariance Invariance
          %p
            The Kontsevich integral is an invariant of
            %span.newWikiWord
              Morse knots
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Morse+knots"} ?
            but is not quite a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+invariant"} knot invariant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(H)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is the “humped” unknot. Therefore, it can be made in to a genuine knot invariant via the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I(K) = \frac{Z(K)}{Z(H)^{c/2}}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is the number of critical points of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %strong final
            Kontsevich integral (and the other the
            %strong preliminary
            one).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+invariant"} Vassiliev invariant
            %li
              %p
